      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Nexus-7 Optical Proximity Sensor Quick-Start Guide\n\n## Overview\nThe Nexus-7 Optical Proximity Sensor is a versatile device designed to measure distances with high precision. It operates within a voltage range of 3.3V to 5V DC and communicates through a 4-pin header interface.\n\n## Specifications\n- **Voltage:** 3.3V - 5V DC\n- **Connection:** 4-pin header (VCC, GND, OUT, Enable)\n- **Detection Range:** 2cm to 40cm\n- **Output Type:** Analog voltage proportional to distance\n\n## Safety Precautions\n- **Warning:** Avoid exposure to direct sunlight and moisture to prevent damage.\n\n## Calibration\nBefore deploying the sensor, ensure it is calibrated in a stable environment to guarantee accurate measurements.\n\n## Usage\nConnect the sensor to your device using the 4-pin header interface. The sensor outputs an analog voltage that is proportional to the measured distance within its detection range.\n\nFor more detailed information and troubleshooting, refer to the full technical manual.",
